info.exam:
The final assessment has two components:

• Team-based face-to-face prototype

During the face-to-face week, students work in teams to design and implement a Remix-based smart contract prototype for a real-world blockchain use case.

• Individual online frontend integration

During the online follow-up, each student individually extends the smart contract idea toward a simple decentralized application interface. The individual work must show how a frontend connects to a smart contract using ABI, contract address, MetaMask and ethers.js.

For the individual online component, each student must submit:

· one simple frontend connected to a smart contract, implemented for example in CodePen, plain
HTML/CSS/JavaScript or another simple web environment approved by the teacher;

· a demo scenario showing wallet connection and smart contract interaction;

· at least one read-only call from the frontend;

· at least one state-changing transaction from the frontend;

· a short individual presentation explaining the application purpose, the smart contract functions used, the frontend interaction flow, the role of MetaMask, the on-chain/off-chain data and the limitations of the solution.

The team prototype developed during the face-to-face week may be used as the starting point, but the online frontend integration and final explanation must be completed individually.

info.objectives:
The course aims to enable design and engineering students to:
• Understand and outline machine learning systems as socio-technical systems;
• Identify and use values to drive the design of machine learning systems;
• Anticipate possible impacts of machine learning systems in practical, personal, social, cultural, and eco-systemic dimensions;
• Identify and exploit the core characteristics and capabilities of machine learning systems in suitable applications;
• Generate relevant, consistent, effective, ethically acceptable, sustainable, and desirable design concepts including machine learning systems;
• Communicate and collaborate in an interdisciplinary teams to develop a machine learning system.

